tengine/godot/issues/111592#issuecomment-3397809651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111592","id":3397809651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KhnXz","user":{"login":"madsbangh","id":2969321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjkzMjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2969321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh","html_url":"https://github.com/madsbangh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madsbangh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T14:40:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T20:15:25Z","body":"> What happens when running the project with `--headless`? Running the game project with a scene isn't necessarily supported, it doesn't support any rendering, so it would need to be set up specifically for that\n\nThanks for the quick reply.\n\n- When just running `godot --headless` in the project directory, we get no errors\n- Likewise when we set `--headless` as the command like argument in the debug settings, it works,\n- Only when the second (or third or forth...) run instance has the --headless argument, we get the crash.\n\nEdit: the second case seems to cause the issue as well, if the game is not embedded\n\nFor context, we are developing a multiplayer game, which starts in server mode when it is headless. Our workflow has been to have one of the run instances be --headless,